{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>The firstborn according to his birthright.</b> He would strike the goblet and say: Reuven, Shimon, Levi, and Yehudah, Yissachar and Zevulun — sons of one mother — seat yourselves in this order according to their births, and likewise all of them. When he reached Binyamin, he said: this one has no mother and I have no mother — let him sit beside me. Immediately <b>the men marveled, each one to his fellow.</b> This is the Midrash of our Rabbis, of blessed memory." "<b>And you should ask:</b> what did they suppose about the goblet? If you say that the goblet was among them like the work of vessels made for telling hours or by the wisdom of the stars and the constellations — throughout all the land of Egypt they were accustomed to this greatly, and it would not have been for them a matter of wonder. Rather, it appears that there was a renewed wisdom among them in the recognition of voices, for it is well known that in a sound speech is intermingled for one who understands the wisdom; and so they said: voice (קול) and breath (רוח) and speech (דבור). And as our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said concerning the sound heard in the grain stalks in the days of Nisan, at the hour when the wind does not blow — for that movement is praise and acknowledgment to the Holy One, blessed be He — and this is what our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: from where do we know that the grain stalks sing song? As it is said (Psalms 65:14): ״יתרועעו אף ישירו״. And in that movement there is a sound, and in that sound speech is intermingled for one who understands that wisdom. And therefore the brothers of Yosef supposed that through the striking of the goblet, speech was intermingled with the sound, and the speech is not heard and understood except by the master of that wisdom alone. And therefore it says <b>and the men marveled, each one to his fellow</b>, for the matter was not among the wisdoms common among them; rather it was a renewed wisdom and they marveled at it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:07.808796731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}